<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Node.js on Winner's Dev Notes</title><link>https://releaseleaf.com/tags/node.js/</link><description>Recent content in Node.js on Winner's Dev Notes</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 03 Jul 2024 22:50:30 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://releaseleaf.com/tags/node.js/rss.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Find Unreferenced Cocos Creator Images with UUID Checks and Node.js</title><link>https://releaseleaf.com/fiuncocrim.html</link><pubDate>Wed, 03 Jul 2024 22:50:30 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://releaseleaf.com/fiuncocrim.html</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Old projects often accumulate images that are no longer referenced. Removing confirmed unused files reduces project size and simplifies asset management.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;For a single image, right-click it in Cocos Creator and inspect its UUID references. Also search code for dynamic references before deleting it.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;For larger projects, this Node.js script compares image &lt;code&gt;.meta&lt;/code&gt; UUIDs with UUIDs found in prefab files:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-0-1"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-0-1"&gt; 1&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-0-2"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-0-2"&gt; 2&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-0-3"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-0-3"&gt; 3&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-0-4"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-0-4"&gt; 4&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id="hl-0-5"&gt;&lt;a class="lnlinks" href="#hl-0-5"&gt; 5&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt" id